+# Bug Assessment: Inventory is not enforced across carts, checkout, cancellation, and product availability
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00Z
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: high
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+Merchants report that ordered stock is often unchanged or another product's stock is decremented; cancellation does not restore stock; carts and checkout accept quantities above stock; and zero-stock products remain available. The requested behavior covers anonymous/authenticated checkout, cart creation and updates, atomic multi-update, one-time cancellation restoration, status conflicts, and v2 product availability.
+
+## Symptom
+
+Inventory operations are not consistently tied to the ordered product and do not enforce stock atomically. Expected behavior is that the `quantity` exposed by `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}` is reserved/decremented and restored exactly once, with 409 Conflict for over-stock cart or checkout changes and canceled-order status transitions.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Create products with distinct availability quantities and place an order containing them; observe that checkout inventory handling can resolve the wrong product and loops over all availability records.
+2. Attempt checkout or a cart quantity update above available stock; observe that the current checkout path logs inventory mismatch and cart paths save without a stock-capacity check.
+3. Set an order status to `CANCELED`, repeat it, or attempt another status; observe that `OrderFacadeImpl.updateOrderStatus` only changes status/history and does not restore or protect inventory.
+4. Retrieve a zero-quantity product through v2 by SKU; the v2 facade delegates directly to the mapper without deriving availability from stock.
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java:146-214` — processes payment and persists the order before inventory validation; uses `productService.getById(orderProduct.getId())`, logs insufficient stock, and decrements every availability row.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java:189-220, 756-1010` — cart creation/addition and single/multi updates save quantities without validating aggregate quantity against product stock; exception mapping does not provide the required 409 response.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java:1624-1647` — status updates are not inventory-aware and permit transitions away from canceled orders.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java:343-391, 402-470, 494-518` — both checkout endpoints currently map failures to generic 503/runtime errors rather than a stock conflict and need consistent conflict propagation.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/product/ProductFacadeV2Impl.java:90-111` and readable product population/mapping — v2 lookup does not force `available`/`canBePurchased` false when effective stock is zero.
+- `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/cart/ShoppingCartAPIIntegrationTest.java` and core order tests — existing coverage exercises basic cart/order flows but not stock isolation, atomic rejection, restoration, or availability transitions.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+**High confidence.** Inventory mutation is implemented as an after-the-fact loop in order creation with an incorrect identifier and no transaction-safe preflight; stock shortages are explicitly not thrown. Cart mutations have no effective-stock validation, and status updates have no inventory transition logic. Product availability is driven independently of the quantity exposed by the product API. These code paths explain the reported symptoms directly.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Introduce a shared inventory service/transactional helper that resolves each ordered/cart product by SKU or the actual product relation, computes the effective stock represented by the product's `quantity`, validates all requested quantities before any persistence, and applies each mutation to only that product's inventory. Checkout should preflight the complete cart, return a typed 409 conflict on any shortage, then create the order and decrement stock atomically for both checkout endpoints.
+
+Use the same validation for cart creation, single updates, and multi-updates; validate a prospective full cart before saving so multi-update is all-or-nothing, while zero/removal/lowering remains allowed. Add cancellation transition logic keyed by order status/history or a persisted restoration marker so restoration occurs once, and reject transitions out of canceled with 409. Derive v2 `available` and `canBePurchased` from merchant availability AND positive effective stock, preserving merchant-unavailable as unavailable.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderService.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartApi.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/product/ProductFacadeV2Impl.java`
+- relevant exception handling and integration/unit test files under `sm-core/src/test` and `sm-shop/src/test`
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+
+- Checkout with multiple products decrements only matching stock by exact ordered quantities.
+- Any checkout shortage returns 409 and leaves order, stock, and cart unchanged.
+- Cart add/single/multi update rejects over-stock atomically; lowering/removal succeeds.
+- Cancellation restores each order product exactly once; canceled orders reject later statuses with 409; other transitions do not change stock.
+- v2 product output switches both flags off at zero stock and back on when replenished, while merchant-unavailable remains false.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Checkout and cancellation must be transactional and concurrency-safe to prevent overselling or double restoration.
+- Existing exception-to-HTTP mappings currently use generic runtime errors and may need a dedicated 409 exception/handler without changing unrelated API errors.
+- Products can have multiple availability records/variants; the implementation must preserve the API's defined stock quantity and avoid decrementing unrelated records.
+- Existing orders created before the fix may not have an explicit restoration marker; repeated cancellation must be guarded using status/history or a compatible persisted marker.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: none for the requested behavior; implementation should follow the product API's effective quantity semantics.]
