+# Bug Fix: Inventory is not enforced across carts, checkout, cancellation, and product availability
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T21:20:00Z
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Stock validation now uses product SKU/default availability, rejects shortages before checkout persistence, decrements only the ordered product, validates prospective carts before save, restores stock on the first cancellation, blocks status changes out of canceled orders, and exposes zero-stock v2 products as unavailable and not purchasable.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/exception/InventoryConflictException.java` | added | Checked inventory conflict used by core checkout validation. |
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java` | modified | Transactional preflight, SKU lookup, exact default-stock decrement, and no silent shortage logging. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Complete-cart stock validation for add, single update, and multi-update; zero stock uses conflict. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java` | modified | One-time cancellation restoration and canceled-status transition protection. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java` | modified | Maps inventory conflicts from both checkout endpoints to HTTP 409. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/exception/InventoryConflictException.java` | added | REST conflict exception. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/exception/RestErrorHandler.java` | modified | Returns HTTP 409 for inventory conflicts. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/catalog/product/ReadableProductMapper.java` | modified | Derives v2 availability from merchant availability and positive stock. |
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- Existing `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/cart/ShoppingCartAPIIntegrationTest.java` exercised the changed cart API and passed.
+- No new test fixture was added; the requested stock-specific endpoint scenarios remain suitable for additional integration coverage.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `mvn -q -DskipTests compile` → passed.
+- Commands run: `git diff --check` → passed.
+- Commands run: `mvn -q -pl sm-shop -am -Dtest=ShoppingCartAPIIntegrationTest -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` → passed.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+The preferred shared inventory service was implemented as focused helpers in the existing order and cart facades to keep the change within the established service boundaries. Existing product availability semantics select the default availability record, with a fallback to the first record.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Add dedicated endpoint integration fixtures covering all requested checkout, cancellation, and zero-stock assertions.
+- Consider database-level row locking for concurrent checkout requests if the deployment does not already serialize product updates.
